# The original, from the Monroe Institute of Applied Sciences Gateway
# Intermediate Workbook (1977) -- the CIA FOIA release. Longer than the settled
# form: "to those who follow me" rather than "near and close to me", and a
# closing protection clause the other forms leave out.
#
# Offered, not prescribed. Protection here is a thing you may want, not a thing
# the exercise requires.
#
# Said in phrases, with a pause after each for the listener to repeat it, as
# in the settled form. The workbook's wording is unchanged.

@segment   affirmation-1977
@title     The Gateway Affirmation — 1977 original
@levels    F10
@family    affirmation
@fixed
@duration  ~2m30s

say Say in your mind. Say to yourself.
pause 4
say I am more than my physical body.
pause 3.5
say Because I am more than physical matter,
pause 3.5
say I can perceive that which is greater than the physical world.
pause 6
say Therefore, in these exercises,
pause 2.5
say I deeply desire to expand,
pause 3
say to experience,
pause 2
say to know,
pause 2
say to understand,
pause 2
say to control,
pause 2
say to use such greater energies and energy systems
pause 3.5
say as may be beneficial and constructive to me,
pause 3.5
say and to those who follow me.
pause 8
say Also during these exercises,
pause 2.5
say I deeply desire the help and cooperation,
pause 3.5
say the assistance, the understanding,
pause 2.5
say of those individuals whose wisdom, development, and experience
pause 3.5
say are equal or greater than my own.
pause 8
say I ask their guidance and protection
pause 3
say from any influence or any source
pause 3
say that might provide me with less than my stated desires.
pause 6
say I now protect myself as may be needed from such influence,
pause 5
say and reject any source
pause 2.5
say that may restrain me from my stated desires.
pause 10
